# Incident Response Runbooks

- Preserve stable error classes and operationally meaningful failure signals when changing error handling.
- When introducing a new critical failure mode, define how it maps to detection, mitigation, and follow-up actions.
- Favor error responses and logs that help operators identify the correct runbook quickly.
- Do not remove or rename important error classes without updating dashboards, alerts, and runbook references.
- Reliability and security-sensitive changes should keep incident response practical, not just technically correct.
